From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] app: keep game power mode on while a game is in the foreground

GameManagerService turns Mode.GAME on when a game's uid reaches
PROCESS_STATE_TOP. Since the disableGameModeWhenAppTop rollout it also
tracks the other uids in the foreground and turns GAME off as soon as
one of them joins a game there: an app next to the game in split screen
or in a freeform window, or for a moment another app's activity that
the game opens, such as a share sheet. GAME comes back on when that app
leaves the foreground. Likewise, a game that joins an app already in the
foreground does not turn GAME on until that app leaves.

On this device GAME drives the automatic game settings: while a game is
in the foreground, palm rejection is turned off and performance mode on
(device/huawei/gaokun3/power/powerhint.json and the Parts switches).
They should stay on while any game is visible, so track games only
again: GAME on when the first game reaches the foreground, off when the
last one leaves it. Nothing else in GameManagerService used the set of
other foreground uids.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [device-specific policy]
